                },
                "message": "Fix sorted() optimiser crash on typeless argument\n\n_handle_simple_function_sorted() dereferenced ``arg.type`` when picking\nbetween ``__Pyx_PySequence_ListKeepNew`` and ``PySequence_List``, but\n``arg.type`` is None for nodes such as a top-level ``or`` expression\nduring EarlyReplaceBuiltinCalls. That regressed after the refactor in\nGH-7543 replaced the earlier ``arg.type in (...)`` membership check,\nwhich was silently None-safe, with ``arg.type.is_pylist_type`` on the\nsame branch.\n\nGuard the check so a None type falls through to the safe\nPySequence_List path and add a regression test covering the reported\n``sorted(x.attr or [])`` and ``sorted(mapping.get(...) or [])`` shapes.\n\nCloses #7957",
